@barryfamgoon @grohmmz @TheEllenShow @mcuban No, a $DOGE transaction costs you 1 $DOGEcoin to process in the blockchain.

Processing fees go to miners. This is how cryptocurrency works. 

So, when $DOGE = a ridiculous price like $.30 you need enough $DOGE to pay the sale price and then another $DOGEcoin to process it.
